course: dictionary
lesson: 9424
title: Squirt: a verb and a noun
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Squirt is a verb when you do it: to squirt is to make liquid shoot out in a thin, fast stream from a small hole. «The gummy sweets are made by squirting hot syrup into shapes.» The syrup is pushed out fast through a small opening.
explain: Squirt is a noun when it is a thing: a squirt is a thin stream of liquid, or a small amount of it. «He added a squirt of lemon juice.» Here squirt names the small amount.
explain: Careful: «a little squirt» is an informal and slightly rude name for a small or annoying young person. Do not use it to call people names.
explain: Use the context to check. Look for a hole, a fast stream or a small amount. Then put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: «Squirt» means to make liquid shoot out in a thin, fast stream from a small hole.
fact: A squirt can also mean a thin stream of liquid, or a small amount of it.
fact: Octopuses, squid and cuttlefish squirt ink to hide or to make a fake blob while they jet away.
fact: Gummy sweets are made by squirting hot syrup into shapes pressed in trays of cornflour.
fact: In science, squirting shows that pressure pushes liquid out of a small hole fast.
exercise: «Gummy sweets are made by squirting hot syrup into shapes.» What does squirting mean here? | Mixing with cornflour | *Forcing liquid out in a thin, fast stream | Pressing into a tray to cool | Drying in the sun
exercise: Dad says «You little squirt!» to his son who splashed him. What does it mean? | A tall, grown-up man | A type of ink | *An informal, slightly rude name for a small, annoying young person
exercise: «He added a squirt of lemon juice.» Which word is the noun? | of | *squirt | lemon | added
test: «The octopus squirted a cloud of ink and jetted away.» Why did it squirt the ink? | To grow bigger | To make pasta black | *To hide while it escaped | To wash its shell
test: Which word in «a squirt of washing-up liquid» is the noun? | *squirt | of | washing-up | a and of
exam: Which sentence uses squirt as a noun? | «Octopuses squirt ink.» | *«Add a squirt of ketchup.» | «Squirting is fun.» | «The water squirted out of the hole.»
